# Environment-specific patterns for the pre-commit hook.
#
# Copy to .githooks/secret-patterns.local (which is gitignored) and add the
# strings you want to keep out of the repo. Each non-comment, non-blank line
# is a regex (matched case-insensitively against staged additions).
#
# Common categories:
#   - Internal IPs / CIDRs (Tailscale, RFC1918, etc.)
#   - Internal TLDs (e.g., .corp, .lab)
#   - Worker / serverless subdomains
#   - Machine hostnames
#   - 1Password vault names you don't want leaked
#
# Examples (replace with your own; commit nothing real here):
#   100\.122\.\d+
#   \.lab\.example
#   workers\.dev
#   host-[abc][^0-9]
